/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  ammoniaRate01_dyson_simon -- the ammonia synthesis rate law on the bench.

  THE PACKAGE BELOW IS A FORMALITY AND SAYS SO.  `ammoniaRateBench` asks the
  correlation object for a rate; it never touches the thermophysical package,
  because Dyson & Simon carry their OWN fugacity coefficients (Eqs 6-8) and
  their OWN equilibrium constant (Eq 2, after Gillespie & Beattie).  That is
  the point of the case rather than an omission: the rate law is an
  INDEPENDENT source, and comparing it with what Choupo's own SRK + Gibbs
  minimisation says is a comparison between two sources instead of a model
  checking itself.  See README.md section 4 -- they agree to 0.63 %.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
application  choupoProps;
tier         tutorial;
description  "The ammonia synthesis rate of Dyson & Simon (1968) as a cited correlation object: Eq 19's pseudo-homogeneous rate, Eq 39's effectiveness factor over Table I's three tabulated pressures, Eq 40, with a declared 150-300 atm window, an announced pressure interpolation and five verify() anchors that each state whether they are THEORY or ARITHMETIC. It locates the LOCUS OF MAXIMUM RATE at three conversions and shows it descending -- the curve ammonia03_quench_converter zigzags about -- and evaluates the rate at that converter's own bed states.";
verbosity    3;
